    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a bridge for me—both as a tool to solve problems and as a subject that demands precision. My parents, both PhDs in STEM fields, instilled curiosity early, but my relationship evolved into one of respectful challenge. It’s not just about numbers; it’s about patterns, logic, and the way equations reveal hidden truths. Though I find it rigorous, I see it as an essential skill for problem-solving in economics or physics.",
